#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119561 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119745 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef2c4b9b-cf73-56d1-96b1-73f48b50ed7b" :knowledge-point/title "Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length Given Its Arc Length"}] :question/id #uuid "9b2026e3-781b-5e73-8dc2-0e8f2789fe67" :question/math-academy-id "e-3065" :question/problem "Consider the curve  $\\mathbf r(t)=\\left\\langle 2t-1 ,\\: 8t+2 ,\\: -2t \\right\\rangle, \\, t \\geq 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $\\mathbf{r}(0)$ to $\\mathbf{r}(t)$ is given by $s=6\\sqrt{2}t.$ Find $\\mathbf R(s),$ the parametrization of the curve by its arc length $s.$" :question/worked-solution "First, since  $s=6\\sqrt{2}t,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6\\sqrt{2}t & =s \\\\ t & =\\frac{s}{6\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ t & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vector function that pametrizes the curve $\\mathbf r(t)$ by its arc length $s,$ with $s \\geq 0,$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{12}) \\\\  & =⟨2(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{12})-1,\\,8(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{12})+2,\\,-2(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{12})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{6}-1,\\,\\frac{4\\sqrt{2}s}{6}+2,\\,-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{6}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}⟨\\sqrt{2}s-6,\\,4\\sqrt{2}s+12,\\,-\\sqrt{2}s⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119562 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119746 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aecbb8b-bda3-5956-9b0f-98509330a84d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length"}] :question/id #uuid "74f33486-6391-5ec0-8a5b-bb51c9af2d55" :question/math-academy-id "e-3066" :question/problem "What is the parametrization of the curve  $\\mathbf r(t)=2(t\\cos{t}-\\sin{t})\\,\\mathbf i+2(t\\sin{t}+\\cos{t})\\,\\mathbf j, \\, t \\geq 0$ by its arc length $s?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $\\mathbf{r}'(t)$ and its magnitude $\\|\\mathbf{r}'(t)\\|\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j \\\\  & =2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+2(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j \\\\  & =-2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =|2t|\\sqrt{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that in the last step, we removed the absolute value bars since $t>0.$ \n\nNext, we calculate the arc length of the curve from $0$ to $t\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}‖{r}^{′}(u)‖\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}2u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={u}^{2}{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & ={t}^{2}-0 \\\\  & ={t}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $s=t^2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & =s \\\\ t & =\\pm \\sqrt{s} \\\\ t & =\\sqrt{s},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ntaking the positive root because $t>0.$  \n\nFinally, the vector function that parametrizes $\\mathbf r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\sqrt{s}) \\\\  & =2(\\sqrt{s}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{s}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{s})\\,i+2(\\sqrt{s}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{s}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{s})\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119563 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119747 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc7343e3-fa7d-58c8-b4c7-49ef5b85110b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Unit Tangent Given the Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length"}] :question/id #uuid "48350682-3ad0-5311-bb47-782ec454390c" :question/math-academy-id "e-3067" :question/problem "Given the curve  $\\mathbf r(t)=\\cos{t}\\,\\mathbf i - \\sin{t}\\,\\mathbf j+\\sqrt{3}t\\,\\mathbf k, \\, t \\geq 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $\\mathbf r(0)$ to $\\mathbf r(t)$ is given by $s=2t,$ find the corresponding unit tangent $\\mathbf{T}(s),$ parametrized by $s.$" :question/worked-solution "First, since $s=2t,$ we have that $t=\\dfrac{s}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the vector function $\\mathbf R(s)$ that parametrizes $\\mathbf r(t)$ by its arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{2}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})\\,j+\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\frac{s}{2}k \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}s}{2}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, since the curve is parametrized by its arc length $s,$ the unit tangent can be found as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf T(s) = \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}s}\\mathbf R(s).\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}))\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}))j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}s}{2})k \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})\\,i-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})\\,i-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})\\,j+\\sqrt{3}\\,k).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262811 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119745 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef2c4b9b-cf73-56d1-96b1-73f48b50ed7b" :knowledge-point/title "Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length Given Its Arc Length"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e1fe70b-f9e8-5e14-95bd-936e4e6cefc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(s+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s)]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260006} {:answer/id #uuid "174557aa-b7d9-5229-9f98-28ccb93a8901" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(s+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(s+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260078} {:answer/id #uuid "2c8c4418-1037-56d1-b0a9-ef14f6a55e38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(s+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260275} {:answer/id #uuid "76f3812d-d66e-52ea-96bd-1ff609fa35c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}s\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s)]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260914} {:answer/id #uuid "b2d052fe-6c22-51b8-9ad5-eac40c0785c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261454}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c8c4418-1037-56d1-b0a9-ef14f6a55e38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(s+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260275} :answer-field/id #uuid "d38f3ab6-9be0-5e12-942e-e5d33286db0e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262492}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "10934b16-caa8-5843-93a5-554278b82678" :question/math-academy-id "q-127687" :question/problem "Consider the curve $r(t)=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}⟨{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s={e}^{t}-1.$ Given that $R(s)$ is the parametrization of the given curve by its arc length $s,$ what is the $x$-component of $R?$" :question/worked-solution "First, since $s={e}^{t}-1,$ we have that $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1).$\n\nThe vector function that pametrizes the curve $r(t)$ by its arc length $s,$ with $s\\ge 0,$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}⟨{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)}\\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)],\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)]⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(s+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)],\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(s+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)]⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, the $x$-component of $R$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(s+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443544 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119745 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef2c4b9b-cf73-56d1-96b1-73f48b50ed7b" :knowledge-point/title "Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length Given Its Arc Length"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18b22410-7856-5e1a-acc1-6826159d44dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{4}),\\,2-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{4})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443491} {:answer/id #uuid "1efba70b-6e3e-5b18-88b3-cce733abfbee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}),\\,2-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443492} {:answer/id #uuid "9b9add6d-7ad1-521a-b998-2bbe4dbdbf01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6s),\\,2-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6s)⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443510} {:answer/id #uuid "ae297d72-79f9-5500-a313-64fff1a8859b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{12}),\\,2-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{12})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443516} {:answer/id #uuid "fa66aa49-7286-5817-af4c-b29349ada577" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3s),\\,2-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3s)⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443533}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1efba70b-6e3e-5b18-88b3-cce733abfbee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}),\\,2-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443492} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe722847-9990-513e-91c0-d8fbc2f2c414" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443541}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3ffd9e9c-d842-5a8a-82a2-58996823be61" :question/math-academy-id "q-127692" :question/problem "Consider the curve $r(t)=⟨3\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t,\\,2-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s=12t.$ Find $R(s),$ the parametrization of the curve by its arc length $s.$" :question/worked-solution "First, since $s=12t,$ we have that $t=\\frac{s}{12}.$\n\nThe vector function that pametrizes the curve $r(t)$ by its arc length $s,$ with $s\\ge 0,$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{12}) \\\\  & =⟨3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{s}{12}),\\,2-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{s}{12})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}),\\,2-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443543 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119745 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef2c4b9b-cf73-56d1-96b1-73f48b50ed7b" :knowledge-point/title "Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length Given Its Arc Length"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0078bb74-f290-5ea7-a214-52b9d695f5aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2s})+3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2s})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443489} {:answer/id #uuid "90c29a1a-cd28-5b50-b2a0-d5a7e09bc382" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2s})+\\sqrt{2s}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2s})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443508} {:answer/id #uuid "bdd6f943-95f7-5873-b8a8-4d4dc0f6b355" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2s})+\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2s})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443518} {:answer/id #uuid "e86fc481-fc66-5c0e-8cd5-654a6782aa39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2s}}{3})+\\frac{\\sqrt{2s}}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2s}}{3})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443528} {:answer/id #uuid "eeb7902b-1060-5a35-9399-e7e8e0a37d2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2s}}{9})+\\frac{\\sqrt{2s}}{9}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2s}}{9})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443531}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90c29a1a-cd28-5b50-b2a0-d5a7e09bc382" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2s})+\\sqrt{2s}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2s})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443508} :answer-field/id #uuid "b84fca7e-39f0-5846-a5a5-8d1c1f76b531" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443537}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "16cdbada-67e8-5de1-a9af-81171c0d9ab3" :question/math-academy-id "q-127693" :question/problem "Consider the curve $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t-3t\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t+3t\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s=\\frac{9}{2}{t}^{2}.$ Given that $R(s)$ is the parametrization of the given curve by its arc length $s,$ what is the $y$-component of $R?$" :question/worked-solution "First, since $s=\\frac{9}{2}{t}^{2},$ we have that $t=\\frac{\\sqrt{2s}}{3}.$\n\nThe vector function that pametrizes the curve $r(t)$ by its arc length $s,$ with $s\\ge 0,$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{\\sqrt{2s}}{3}) \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2s}}{3})-3\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2s}}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2s}}{3}),\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2s}}{3})+3\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2s}}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2s}}{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2s})-\\sqrt{2s}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2s}),\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2s})+\\sqrt{2s}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2s})⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, the $y$-component of $R$ is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\sqrt{2s})+\\sqrt{2s}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\sqrt{2s}).\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443546 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119747 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc7343e3-fa7d-58c8-b4c7-49ef5b85110b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Unit Tangent Given the Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32ff6b62-7151-50dd-84b9-f0682178bc3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T(s)=\\frac{1}{3}⟨2,\\,1,\\,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443494} {:answer/id #uuid "5cbd1f61-356b-5e0e-97c4-264d421a9397" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T(s)=\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6}⟨2,\\,1,\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443499} {:answer/id #uuid "74144c16-17c1-5293-9b2e-c5a9eeff8750" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T(s)=\\frac{1}{3}⟨1,\\,-2,\\,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443504} {:answer/id #uuid "74bae46f-6326-5411-928d-8a2bfd164ba4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T(s)=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}⟨-1,\\,-1,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443505} {:answer/id #uuid "e25ed8bf-2138-5064-9377-39d74381a566" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T(s)=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}⟨1,\\,1,\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443527}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32ff6b62-7151-50dd-84b9-f0682178bc3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T(s)=\\frac{1}{3}⟨2,\\,1,\\,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443494} :answer-field/id #uuid "65648327-28cf-5416-8e2f-6a1fc5001bde" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443535}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7ba59ca0-21f4-55ed-9a11-93e0f28f7d7a" :question/math-academy-id "q-127707" :question/problem "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2}+3,\\,\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{2},\\,1-{t}^{2}⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s=\\frac{3{t}^{2}}{2},$ find the corresponding unit tangent $T(s),$ parametrized by $s.$" :question/worked-solution "First, since $s=\\frac{3{t}^{2}}{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3{t}^{2}}{2} & =s \\\\ {t}^{2} & =\\frac{2s}{3} \\\\ t & =\\sqrt{\\frac{2s}{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector function $R(s)$ that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\sqrt{\\frac{2s}{3}}) \\\\  & =⟨{(\\sqrt{\\frac{2s}{3}})}^{2}+3,\\,\\frac{1}{2}{(\\sqrt{\\frac{2s}{3}})}^{2}\\,,1-{(\\sqrt{\\frac{2s}{3}})}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2s}{3}+3,\\,\\frac{s}{3},\\,1-\\frac{2s}{3}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nNow, since the curve is parameterized by its arc length $s$, the unit tangent can be found as\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s).\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{2s}{3}+3),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{s}{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(1-\\frac{2s}{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{1}{3},\\,-\\frac{2}{3}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨2,\\,1,\\,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443549 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119746 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aecbb8b-bda3-5956-9b0f-98509330a84d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88524411-7322-5c13-a0d6-4635b37af634" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨\\frac{s}{5},\\,\\frac{4s}{5},\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443507} {:answer/id #uuid "9cf6e55a-b413-5aa8-ab0c-0067c9c7f83b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{5}},\\,\\frac{2s}{\\sqrt{5}},\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443511} {:answer/id #uuid "c64215ca-c1b2-57b5-bdd6-c53bbb436663" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨s,\\,\\frac{4s}{3},\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443520} {:answer/id #uuid "caf2317e-01bb-53d6-bd84-e85f0344d156" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨\\frac{s}{3},\\,\\frac{2s}{3},\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443523} {:answer/id #uuid "e10e8c34-d7a5-5c32-a5fb-5487a2156990" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨\\frac{3s}{5},\\,\\frac{4s}{5},\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443526}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e10e8c34-d7a5-5c32-a5fb-5487a2156990" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨\\frac{3s}{5},\\,\\frac{4s}{5},\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443526} :answer-field/id #uuid "369bbd24-91f1-5851-8599-621408e0023b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443534}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f674176f-f4e0-51c5-b4b9-0830e520af3b" :question/math-academy-id "q-127733" :question/problem "What is the parametrization of the curve $r(t)=⟨{t}^{3/2},\\,\\frac{4}{3}{t}^{3/2},\\,1⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ by its arc length $s?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3/2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{4}{3}{t}^{3/2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{1/2},\\,2{t}^{1/2},\\,0⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{1/2})}^{2}+{(2{t}^{1/2})}^{2}+(0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}t+4t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{25}{4}t} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}\\sqrt{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the arc length of the curve from $0$ to $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}‖{r}^{′}(u)‖\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}\\frac{5}{2}\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{t}\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}\\,{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{3}\\sqrt{{t}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $s=\\frac{5}{3}\\sqrt{{t}^{3}},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{3}\\sqrt{{t}^{3}} & =s \\\\ \\sqrt{{t}^{3}} & =\\frac{3s}{5} \\\\ t & ={(\\frac{3s}{5})}^{2/3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector function that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r({(\\frac{3s}{5})}^{2/3}) \\\\  & =⟨{({(\\frac{3s}{5})}^{2/3})}^{3/2},\\,\\frac{4}{3}{({(\\frac{3s}{5})}^{2/3})}^{3/2},\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3s}{5},\\,\\frac{4}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3s}{5},\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3s}{5},\\,\\frac{4s}{5},\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262819 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119746 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aecbb8b-bda3-5956-9b0f-98509330a84d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bc36f85-1102-5b80-a094-c10071f3364c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=\\frac{1}{4}⟨2s,\\,3s,\\,2-\\sqrt{3}\\,s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260408} {:answer/id #uuid "9e30404b-905a-57cd-82cf-234f22d1abc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=\\frac{1}{3}⟨s,\\,2s-3,\\,-2s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261246} {:answer/id #uuid "ad627246-dce6-5769-8332-676206ded725" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=\\frac{1}{4}⟨3s,\\,s,\\,1-\\sqrt{6}\\,s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261393} {:answer/id #uuid "bb67c9f7-2efa-5489-a1d0-6cdfde17faa8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=\\frac{1}{3}⟨s,\\,2s+3,\\,2s-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261525} {:answer/id #uuid "fa040405-81a8-51bd-8162-855fbd609651" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=\\frac{1}{3}⟨2s,\\,s+6,\\,9-2s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262058}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa040405-81a8-51bd-8162-855fbd609651" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=\\frac{1}{3}⟨2s,\\,s+6,\\,9-2s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262058} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a4d7171-4466-5034-b27a-ebb267da9c78" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262254}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "35d19d31-9377-5a1f-a9f6-e8ea15486111" :question/math-academy-id "q-127739" :question/problem "What is the parametrization of the curve $r(t)=⟨{t}^{4},\\,\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{4}+2,\\,3-{t}^{4}⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ by its arc length $s?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{4}+2),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3-{t}^{4})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4{t}^{3},\\,2{t}^{3},\\,-4{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\  & =2{t}^{3}⟨2,\\,1,\\,-2⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =|2{t}^{3}|\\sqrt{{(2)}^{2}+{(1)}^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =2{t}^{3}\\sqrt{4+1+4} \\\\  & =6{t}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the arc length of the curve from $0$ to $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}‖{r}^{′}(u)‖\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}6{u}^{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =6{\\int }_{0}^{t}{u}^{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{u}^{4}\\,{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $s=\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{4}$ and $t\\ge 0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{4} & =s \\\\ {t}^{4} & =\\frac{2s}{3} \\\\ t & =\\sqrt[4]{\\frac{2s}{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector function that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\sqrt[4]{\\frac{2s}{3}}) \\\\  & =⟨{(\\sqrt[4]{\\frac{2s}{3}})}^{4},\\,\\frac{1}{2}{(\\sqrt[4]{\\frac{2s}{3}})}^{4}+2,\\,3-{(\\sqrt[4]{\\frac{2s}{3}})}^{4}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2s}{3},\\,\\frac{s}{3}+2,\\,3-\\frac{2s}{3}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨2s,\\,s+6,\\,9-2s⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120279 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119745 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef2c4b9b-cf73-56d1-96b1-73f48b50ed7b" :knowledge-point/title "Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length Given Its Arc Length"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04e527b9-3209-50d5-aaa3-8bf133b7f3dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=\\frac{1}{7}⟨2s,\\,1-3s,\\,5+6s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312004} {:answer/id #uuid "860b9d1d-8a3f-5f6e-aa07-757fcfca11c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨2s,\\,7+3s,\\,35+6s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313051} {:answer/id #uuid "9cb65002-7c68-5ed0-bc75-f31eba7bc763" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=\\frac{1}{7}⟨2s,\\,7+3s,\\,35+6s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313215} {:answer/id #uuid "9efdae8e-52ac-5d4d-910f-4cc2786f8b6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨2s,\\,7-3s,\\,35+6s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313225} {:answer/id #uuid "bb1543e9-0a7e-55d3-8cb0-c7b5bb91f9d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=\\frac{1}{7}⟨2s,\\,7-3s,\\,35+6s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313433}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb1543e9-0a7e-55d3-8cb0-c7b5bb91f9d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=\\frac{1}{7}⟨2s,\\,7-3s,\\,35+6s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313433} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e94e688-21a1-5bc1-bdf8-2b812cd1d886" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314134}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cd2d22fe-d6c9-55e5-8f32-f782e37e2d9e" :question/math-academy-id "q-33860" :question/problem "Consider the curve $r(t)=⟨2t,\\,1-3t,\\,5+6t⟩$, $t\\ge 0$, for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s=7t.$ Find $R(s),$ the parametrization of the curve by its arc length $s.$" :question/worked-solution "First, since $s=7t$, we have that $t=\\frac{s}{7}.$\n\nThe vector function that pametrizes the curve $r(t)$ by its arc length $s$, with $s\\ge 0$, is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{7}) \\\\  & =⟨2(\\frac{s}{7}),\\,1-3(\\frac{s}{7}),\\,5+6(\\frac{s}{7})⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}⟨2s,\\,7-3s,\\,35+6s⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120287 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119746 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aecbb8b-bda3-5956-9b0f-98509330a84d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03d35f72-203f-50ad-acf8-60daf8ec86f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨\\frac{3s}{10},\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5}),\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443490} {:answer/id #uuid "687213da-1e26-52a8-97ee-db6e4936d9a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨3s\\sqrt{5},\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2s\\sqrt{5}),\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2s\\sqrt{5})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443502} {:answer/id #uuid "a4ac553f-f8dc-540a-b14f-5081633e4785" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨3s,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2s),\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2s)⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443513} {:answer/id #uuid "a7440719-45de-5623-a9fc-402f1704445f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨3s,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5s),\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5s)⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443515} {:answer/id #uuid "cd7758b9-5236-5926-b5ee-c1a0c9406558" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨\\frac{3s}{5},\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2s}{5}),\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2s}{5})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443524}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd7758b9-5236-5926-b5ee-c1a0c9406558" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨\\frac{3s}{5},\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2s}{5}),\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2s}{5})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443524} :answer-field/id #uuid "a151873b-5e83-57f7-8ab2-495a187820b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117861}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "bf7d29a0-f7b5-5ec6-9f09-d4bee4934cb2" :question/math-academy-id "q-33974" :question/problem "What is the parametrization of the curve $r(t)=⟨3t,\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t),\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ by its arc length $s?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t),\\,-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t))^{2}+(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+16{cos}^{2}⁡(2t)+16{sin}^{2}⁡(2t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+16({cos}^{2}⁡(2t)+{sin}^{2}⁡(2t))} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the arc length of the curve from $0$ to $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}‖{r}^{′}(u)‖\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}5\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =5u\\,{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & =5t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $s=5t$, we have that $t=\\frac{s}{5}.$\n\nTherefore, the vector function that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{5}) \\\\  & =⟨3\\cdot \\frac{s}{5},\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{s}{5}),\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{s}{5})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{3s}{5},\\,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2s}{5}),\\,2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2s}{5})⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443548 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119745 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef2c4b9b-cf73-56d1-96b1-73f48b50ed7b" :knowledge-point/title "Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length Given Its Arc Length"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21552ed1-365f-5f5f-9f16-05c0709bc3e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3[{(\\frac{s}{2})}^{3/4}-1]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443493} {:answer/id #uuid "3329a212-2843-5cea-8b79-3333d2a3bf2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{[{(\\frac{s}{4}-1)}^{2/3}+1]}^{2/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443495} {:answer/id #uuid "63ae5483-af4f-5b7e-81e0-1879fd88e830" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[{(\\frac{s}{2})}^{3/2}+1]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443500} {:answer/id #uuid "9188031a-cf46-5bd8-b259-521ae93aa9b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6[{(\\frac{s}{4})}^{2/3}-1]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443509} {:answer/id #uuid "bece495d-d450-5992-940a-15e713087f67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{[{(\\frac{s}{4}+1)}^{2/3}+1]}^{3/2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443519}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9188031a-cf46-5bd8-b259-521ae93aa9b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6[{(\\frac{s}{4})}^{2/3}-1]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443509} :answer-field/id #uuid "93649b9b-4496-5be5-8efe-dc54d74802dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443536}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d79c5095-b4c8-55c2-88ef-92a621d4625c" :question/math-academy-id "q-34887" :question/problem "Consider the curve  $r(t)=(6t-6)\\,i+4(t-1)^{3/2}\\,j+2\\,k,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s=4{t}^{3/2}.$ Given that $R(s)$ is the parameterization of the given curve by its arc length $s,$ what is the $x$-component of $R?$" :question/worked-solution "First, since  $s=4{t}^{3/2}$,  we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & =4{t}^{3/2} \\\\ {t}^{3/2} & =\\frac{s}{4} \\\\ t & ={(\\frac{s}{4})}^{2/3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe vector function that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r({(\\frac{s}{4})}^{2/3}) \\\\  & =[6{(\\frac{s}{4})}^{2/3}-6]\\,i+4{[{(\\frac{s}{4})}^{2/3}-1]}^{3/2}\\,j+2\\,k \\\\  & =6[{(\\frac{s}{4})}^{2/3}-1]\\,i+4{[{(\\frac{s}{4})}^{2/3}-1]}^{3/2}\\,j+2\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, the $x$-component of $R$ is\n\n$$\n6[{(\\frac{s}{4})}^{2/3}-1].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348078 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119746 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aecbb8b-bda3-5956-9b0f-98509330a84d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0deca599-ab0e-52b8-9014-d10ec63b0b37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\,s}{6},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\,s}{6},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\,s}{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345462} {:answer/id #uuid "23e518c4-aa56-56d4-ac96-d8de1b630937" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{3},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{3},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{8}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345680} {:answer/id #uuid "27597662-d72b-58c7-9c73-6d7aa227dbce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{4},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{4},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{8}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345705} {:answer/id #uuid "cee297c6-6c2a-579f-97ba-46b06d834946" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\,s}{2},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\,s}{6},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\,s}{6}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347163} {:answer/id #uuid "e0fdf0bf-0fdc-570c-aed5-7c3e6ec100e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{6},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{6},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347327}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0fdf0bf-0fdc-570c-aed5-7c3e6ec100e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{6},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{6},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347327} :answer-field/id #uuid "329b56ad-7508-5224-a7c6-7d7ef0019f7b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347688}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ec5db497-36ab-565c-9851-a44645728973" :question/math-academy-id "q-78390" :question/problem "What is the parametrization of the curve $r(t)=⟨\\frac{t}{2},\\,\\frac{t}{2},\\,t⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ by its arc length $s?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{t}{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{t}{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\frac{1}{2},\\,1⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{4}+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the arc length of the curve from $0$ to $t:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}‖{r}^{′}(u)‖\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}}\\cdot u{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}}\\,t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $s=\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}}\\,t$,  we have that $t=\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}\\,s.$\n\nTherefore, the vector function that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}\\,s) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}\\,s,\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}\\,s,\\,\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}\\,s⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{6},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{6},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{3}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443547 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119746 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aecbb8b-bda3-5956-9b0f-98509330a84d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33d8185a-6a2a-5892-8eca-d2a40aec6d78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})j-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443496} {:answer/id #uuid "357c3fed-2573-5af2-9a74-38fdbb7e9536" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{4})i+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{4})j-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{4})k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443497} {:answer/id #uuid "7e98db7f-69a7-535b-991b-a8a9c022916b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{4})i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{4})j-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{4})k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443506} {:answer/id #uuid "c8848381-e308-52a4-a707-2d321aed36f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})j-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443521} {:answer/id #uuid "eaaf160a-2424-50be-88b7-1cac758b976c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})i+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})j-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443530}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eaaf160a-2424-50be-88b7-1cac758b976c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})i+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})j-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443530} :answer-field/id #uuid "dff45dea-1e54-5748-adfe-76155f49648f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443540}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a07b5060-561f-5345-8fe4-ea776cd5863a" :question/math-academy-id "q-78400" :question/problem "What is the parametrization of the curve $r(t)=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\,i+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\,j-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\,k,$  $\\,t\\ge 0,$ by its arc length $s?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t))i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t))\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t))k \\\\  & =5\\cdot 4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\,i-4\\cdot 4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\,j+3\\cdot 4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\,k \\\\  & =20\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\,i-16\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\,j+12\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\,k \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(20\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t))}^{2}+{(16\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t))}^{2}+{(12\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{400{cos}^{2}⁡(4t)+256{sin}^{2}⁡(4t)+144{sin}^{2}⁡(4t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{400[{cos}^{2}⁡(4t)+{sin}^{2}⁡(4t)]} \\\\  & =20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the arc length of the curve from $0$ to $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}‖{r}^{′}(u)‖\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}20\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =20u\\,{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & =20t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nNow, since $s=20t$, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & =20t \\\\ t & =\\frac{s}{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector function that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{20}) \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{s}{20})i+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{s}{20})j-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{s}{20})k \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})i+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})j-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{5})k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443545 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119747 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc7343e3-fa7d-58c8-b4c7-49ef5b85110b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Unit Tangent Given the Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69ca1aac-6b11-5376-9937-2208496cced2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}i+\\frac{1}{4}\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443503} {:answer/id #uuid "c9b146bb-770e-5edf-a89a-ddb5a4e69aef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}i+\\frac{1}{2}\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443522} {:answer/id #uuid "d7a63ea5-e82d-58f3-a26d-7d87b25fa26b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}i+\\frac{1}{4}\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443525} {:answer/id #uuid "e925d7f5-a15f-5b03-9457-e819bfb1f793" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}i+\\frac{1}{2}\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443529} {:answer/id #uuid "f0b622e5-528f-57ff-bbcd-8e0d4e03bb0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{12}i+\\frac{1}{8}\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443532}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9b146bb-770e-5edf-a89a-ddb5a4e69aef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}i+\\frac{1}{2}\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443522} :answer-field/id #uuid "de3dc3d1-7e1d-5412-9859-e96e904a13e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443538}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6c7e6c99-f8ae-5d4a-9e7f-5c595417e9ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-78402" :question/problem "Given the curve  $r(t)=(3t-1)\\,i+2t\\,j+\\sqrt{3}t\\,k,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s=4t,$ find the corresponding unit tangent $T(s),$ parametrized by $s.$" :question/worked-solution "First, since $s=4t$, we have that $t=\\frac{s}{4}.$  \n\nTherefore, the vector function $R(s)$ that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{4}) \\\\  & =(3\\cdot \\frac{s}{4}-1)i+(2\\cdot \\frac{s}{4})j+(\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\frac{s}{4})k \\\\  & =(\\frac{3s-4}{4})i+\\frac{s}{2}\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}s}{4}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nNow, since the curve is parametrized by its arc length $s$, the unit tangent can be found as\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s).\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{3s-4}{4})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{s}{2})j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}s}{4})k \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\,i+\\frac{1}{2}\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348079 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119747 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc7343e3-fa7d-58c8-b4c7-49ef5b85110b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Unit Tangent Given the Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c6e8a62-6c5e-5c07-8b38-9629f6e61c66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2}{5},\\,\\frac{3}{5},\\,\\frac{6}{5}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346290} {:answer/id #uuid "6cc9ddc0-286e-5730-8348-630a2c6bfe50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{5},\\,\\frac{3}{5},\\,\\frac{3}{5}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346297} {:answer/id #uuid "9a9bcc86-1dfb-5e38-8fa0-9abbc2ce5363" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2}{7},\\,\\frac{3}{7},\\,\\frac{6}{7}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346701} {:answer/id #uuid "cd5c653c-10ca-5639-86e6-15c284b3313c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2}{14},\\,\\frac{3}{14},\\,\\frac{2}{7}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347148} {:answer/id #uuid "e5ec4efb-ec1e-5eee-8d21-72d1fcfd2de2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{7},\\,\\frac{2}{7},\\,\\frac{3}{7}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347376}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a9bcc86-1dfb-5e38-8fa0-9abbc2ce5363" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2}{7},\\,\\frac{3}{7},\\,\\frac{6}{7}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346701} :answer-field/id #uuid "50e2f562-fc1a-5512-a817-ac49a9aa2b67" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347745}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "80d24151-001d-558c-b4cf-13fe29c86835" :question/math-academy-id "q-78403" :question/problem "Given the curve  $r(t)=⟨2{e}^{t},\\,3{e}^{t},\\,6{e}^{t}⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s=7({e}^{t}-1),$ find the corresponding unit tangent $T(s),$ parametrized by $s.$" :question/worked-solution "First, since $s=7({e}^{t}-1)$, we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{s}{7} & ={e}^{t}-1 \\\\ {e}^{t} & =\\frac{s}{7}+1 \\\\ t & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{s+7}{7}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the vector function $R(s)$ that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{s+7}{7})) \\\\  & =⟨2{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{s+7}{7})},\\,3{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{s+7}{7})},\\,6{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{s+7}{7})}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2\\cdot \\frac{s+7}{7},\\,3\\cdot \\frac{s+7}{7},\\,6\\cdot \\frac{s+7}{7}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2s+14}{7},\\,\\frac{3s+21}{7},\\,\\frac{6s+42}{7}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nNow, since the curve is parametrized by its arc length $s$, the unit tangent can be found as\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s).\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{2s+14}{7}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{3s+21}{7}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{6s+42}{7})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2}{7},\\,\\frac{3}{7},\\,\\frac{6}{7}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393849 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119747 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc7343e3-fa7d-58c8-b4c7-49ef5b85110b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Unit Tangent Given the Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f744694c-a7e5-531b-b1a0-b70a89880b50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{9},\\,\\frac{4}{9},\\,\\frac{8}{9}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393851} {:answer/id #uuid "90720291-67d0-5e1a-b546-8a1aea34b932" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{9},\\,\\frac{2}{9},\\,\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{9}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393852} {:answer/id #uuid "8fcf0b34-e534-51fc-97fb-64d7d6fafa02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{9},\\,\\frac{2}{9},\\,\\frac{1}{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393853} {:answer/id #uuid "07fc2226-9b81-5440-8648-0026a95bbbe8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{18},\\,\\frac{2}{9},\\,\\frac{4}{9}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393854} {:answer/id #uuid "edbdf1ca-35ec-595a-a27c-e608c973c72f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{81},\\,\\frac{4}{81},\\,\\frac{8}{81}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393855}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f744694c-a7e5-531b-b1a0-b70a89880b50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{9},\\,\\frac{4}{9},\\,\\frac{8}{9}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393851} :answer-field/id #uuid "7fefcfb2-453a-5854-be55-e93605da6418" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393850}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "56897adb-706a-5c81-8930-6f2aa15c0be7" :question/math-academy-id "q-78404" :question/problem "Given the curve  $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2},\\,4{t}^{2},\\,8{t}^{2}⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s=9{t}^{2},$ find the corresponding unit tangent $T(s),$ parametrized by $s.$" :question/worked-solution "First, since $s=9{t}^{2}$, we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & =\\frac{s}{9} \\\\ t & =\\frac{\\sqrt{s}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the vector function $R(s)$ that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{\\sqrt{s}}{3}) \\\\  & =⟨{(\\frac{\\sqrt{s}}{3})}^{2},\\,4{(\\frac{\\sqrt{s}}{3})}^{2},\\,8{(\\frac{\\sqrt{s}}{3})}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{s}{9},\\,\\frac{4s}{9},\\,\\frac{8s}{9}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nNow, since the curve is parametrized by its arc length $s$, the unit tangent can be found as\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s).\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{s}{9}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{4s}{9}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{8s}{9})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{9},\\,\\frac{4}{9},\\,\\frac{8}{9}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186443542 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119747 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc7343e3-fa7d-58c8-b4c7-49ef5b85110b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Unit Tangent Given the Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "447ff6ac-8e33-53a7-a4b3-bb9df76bffb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{35}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{7}),\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{14},\\,-\\frac{1}{35}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{7})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443498} {:answer/id #uuid "6486f987-8f88-59d1-a346-9c83d923a1ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{7}),\\,\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{7},\\,-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{7})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443501} {:answer/id #uuid "a1d0d21b-45e7-55b2-a074-9a46fed29092" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{35}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{7}),\\,\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{7},\\,-\\frac{1}{35}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{7})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443512} {:answer/id #uuid "a5c74af9-8ca2-5cca-a7be-75a239dd9ecc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{7}),\\,\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{7},\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{7})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443514} {:answer/id #uuid "b7a1952d-4592-5193-b5f8-225ef704bbd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{5}{7}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{7}),\\,\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{7},\\,-\\frac{5}{7}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{7})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443517}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7a1952d-4592-5193-b5f8-225ef704bbd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{5}{7}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{7}),\\,\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{7},\\,-\\frac{5}{7}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{7})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443517} :answer-field/id #uuid "de6079b3-a0dd-5241-b8ce-a969c300edc5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186443539}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1147fbce-b0d6-511f-b878-2ccccfbc032b" :question/math-academy-id "q-78437" :question/problem "Given the curve  $r(t)=⟨5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,2\\sqrt{6}t,\\,5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s=7t,$ find the corresponding unit tangent $T(s),$ parametrized by $s.$" :question/worked-solution "First, since $s=7t$, we have that $t=\\frac{s}{7}.$\n\nTherefore, the vector function $R(s)$ that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{7}) \\\\  & =⟨5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{7}),\\,2\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\frac{s}{7},\\,5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{7})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{7}),\\,\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}s}{7},\\,5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{7})⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nNow, since the curve is parametrized by its arc length $s$, the unit tangent can be found as\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s).\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{7})),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}s}{7}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{7}))⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{5}{7}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{7}),\\,\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{7},\\,-\\frac{5}{7}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{7})⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
